{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"TrackingPlanTesting","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","title":"TrackingPlanTesting","modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlanTesting"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackingplantesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fail a Swift Testing test when an app’s events no longer match its committed tracking plan, so every change to an event comes with a change to the plan."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracking plan is how the people and services that read an app’s events learn what each event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds, so it is only useful while it matches the events. With this test, a change to an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t pass the app’s tests until the plan is exported again, and reviewers see the change as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON diff of the plan. The test’s report also says which changes would break payloads from released"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app versions or records already stored."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting\/expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" checks a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" against the plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"committed in a directory, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan.check(againstDirectory:)"},{"text":" does. When they differ, it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records a Swift Testing issue whose comment is the check’s report, the same text the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"command prints, and it returns the check either way. A plan that is only out of date fails the test","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a breaking one does: in both cases the committed plan isn’t what exporting the events writes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the product to an app’s test target, so the check runs wherever the app’s tests do. It imports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Swift Testing, so it belongs in test targets only. To run the check from the command line or CI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without a test, use the app’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanCommand"},{"type":"text","text":" executable from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import Testing","import TrackingPlanTesting","","@Test func eventsMatchTheTrackingPlan() throws {","    let directory = URL(fileURLWithPath: #filePath)","        .deletingLastPathComponent()","        .appendingPathComponent(\"TrackingPlan\")","    expectTrackingPlan(try AppTrackingPlan.trackingPlan, matches: directory)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers exporting the plan this test checks."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Checking from a test","anchor":"Checking-from-a-test","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting\/expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)"]}